  "summary": "CRC outreach worklist 'Okafor CRC 2026' (grp-okafor-crc, 4 members), worked under RBC-QM-02 (measurement period 2026).\n\n| Patient | Age end-2026 | Status | Reason / action |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| pt-0009 Elly Trantow | 72 | Open gap | No FIT in 2026, no sDNA-FIT 2024-26, no colonoscopy/flex sig/CT colonography on record. At first she looked excluded (frailty plus donepezil), but Dr. Lin's message (comm-00301) arrived during the work: the Frailty entry (cond-00189) belonged to another patient and is now marked entered in error. Without frailty the exclusion doesn't apply. No nursing home or hospice on record. FIT kit ordered (sr-t0001) and outreach message sent (comm-t0004). |\n| pt-0020 Kelsie Rohan | 52 | Excluded | Hospice episode eoc-00002 ran 2026-06-16 to 2026-08-21 (finished; she revoked hospice to join a clinical trial, per the faxed discharge summary doc-00402). A finished hospice episode in 2026 excludes her. No order, no patient contact. |\n| pt-0022 Tiny Koss | 51 | Open gap | Her only FIT (obs-01732) was corrected during the work: the sample was collected 2025-12-31, not 2026-01-05 (that was the lab's receipt date). That is outside 2026, so it doesn't count. No other screening, no exclusions. FIT kit ordered (sr-t0002) and outreach message sent (comm-t0005). |\n| pt-0024 Delaine MacGyver | 51 | Open gap | Her 2024-06-11 stool DNA-FIT (obs-01871) was withdrawn by Harbor lab as a mislabelled specimen and is now entered in error (doc-00401). The 2025 colonoscopy order sr-00003 was never done, and an order doesn't count. No exclusions and no existing FIT order. FIT kit ordered (sr-t0003) and outreach message sent (comm-t0006). |\n\nAll three FIT orders have a window of 2026-10-23 to 2026-12-31. Each outreach message says the kit is on its way and explains how to collect, date and mail back the sample. None makes claims about past test results.\n\nArrivals (§8): the four items that came in during the work (inbox-a0001 to a0004) were reviewed before any decision was recorded. All four were completed with comments, and three are linked to their order and message. No decision needed correcting. A final check found no further arrivals. Unrelated older inbox items were left untouched.",
